## 2026-11-16 — later changes (appended)

### P005 fix — real 4×4 boards were mis-read as 6×6
- **Files:** `src/tilegrid.py`, `src/ad_close_loop.py`, `src/solve_from_image.py`
- **Why:** `_fit_grid()` required seams to span nearly the whole board, but a 4×4 has only 3
  *internal* seam lines, so the fit always failed and `detect_geometry()` silently returned the 6×6
  default → garbage grid → `NO SOLUTION`.
- **Change:** internal-span rule `(n-2.2)*cell`; accept a single clean gap when ≥3 candidate seams
  exist; mirror one good axis as `seams_x`/`seams_y`; `looks_like_real_board()` accepts those
  sources; the solver retries N ∈ {4,5,6} on the fixed frame when geometry is `default`.
- **Verified:** the wasted board `queue/20261116_152053_no_solution.png` solves at cost 2; 4×4 +
  6×6 regression all solve; tests pass.

### `run_loop.py --wait <minutes>`
- **Files:** `src/run_loop.py`
- **Why:** on TIME_UP the loop exited, so the operator had to restart it by hand. `--wait` polls the
  screenshot with **zero taps** until a real board appears (still does nothing at all on time-up).
- **Verified:** run 004 parked on the Time's Up panel and picked up the next board.

### P006 fix — greyed `Loading ad...` panel accepted as a board
- **Files:** `src/ad_close_loop.py`, `src/run_loop.py`
- **Why:** `looks_like_result()` keyed on the *yellow* CTA, so the disabled grey `Loading ad...`
  variant of the Time's Up panel was missed and a dead board was played.
- **Change:** `looks_like_result()` is now colour-agnostic (wide solid bright band ≥30 rows on the
  game's dark background); `wait_for_board()` also requires a *running clock* (two frames 2.2 s
  apart must differ in the HUD timer).
- **Verified:** loading-ad frame → True; `ad_puzzle_01.png` (Play-Store end card) → False; live
  4×4/6×6 → False; tests pass.

### P007 fix — board behind a rewarded ad could expire unseen (+ false win)
- **Files:** `src/ad_close_loop.py`, `src/run_loop.py`
- **Why:** the reward deals the next board while the end card is still up; the ~80 s creative plus
  slow ad polls let that board's 60 s clock run out. Run 006 captured it with 3 s left, spent 19
  taps, got TIME_UP and mis-logged it as a win.
- **Change:** `clock_is_critical()` red-timer guard (never tap a red-clock board, log `expired`);
  post-tap win confirmed via the UI tree (TIME_UP = timeout, not a win); no residual self-repair on
  a red board; `wait_for_board()` rejects red-clock boards.
- **Verified:** guard matrix (58 s False / 3 s True / 0 s True / 43 s win False); tests pass.

### P007 follow-up — close the ad the moment the reward is paid (screenshot-only)
- **Files:** `src/ad_reward.py` (new), `src/ad_close_loop.py`, `src/test_runtime.py`,
  `Memory/derived/ad_close/templates/*.png` (new)
- **Why:** the fixed `reward_wait=75 s` was the real cost. Run 007's ad reached its end card at 8 s
  and we closed at 72 s — 64 s of the new board's 60 s clock spent on an end card.
- **Change:** the AdMob badge switches from `Reward in N second(s)` to `Reward granted` when the
  reward is paid. `ad_reward.reward_state()` matches that string on an **edge map** (colour- and
  polarity-invariant, no OCR, no `uiautomator dump`, 0.03 s warm). `close_ad()` checks it right after
  each screenshot, before the dump, and closes as soon as it is true (≥4 s in); the old timing path
  stays as a fallback for creatives with no badge. `poll_s` 2.5 → 1.2 s, post-tap settle 3 → 1.2 s.
- **Verified:** over 277 archived ad frames — granted 0.977-1.000, `Reward in 1 second` 0.406-0.408,
  no-badge ads 0.085-0.255, boards ≈ -0.02. New `test_reward_granted_fast_close` closes at 5 s with
  `reward_wait=75`; `test_reward_wait` still proves a countdown badge is never tapped early.

### P008 fix — close early by rule change (operator decision)
- **Files:** `src/ad_close_loop.py`, `src/test_runtime.py`
- **Why:** the P008 creative (Play-Store style end card) has **no** `Reward granted` badge, so the
  badge detector never fires and the 75 s fallback cost another board. Operator ruling: the reward is
  to be treated as already confirmed, so close earlier.
- **Change:** `close_ad(early_close_s=18.0)` closes at 18 s with no confirmation; badge-granted
  (>= 4 s) and frozen-end-card paths still close sooner; `reward_wait` is now only a safety cap.
  Badge score logged every poll.
- **Verified:** `test_early_close_no_badge` closes the Twin Tales end card at 17 s; all tests pass.

### P009 fix - never tap ad content; BACK instead of blind coordinates
- **Files:** `src/ad_close_loop.py`, `src/test_runtime.py`
- **Why:** at the 18 s close deadline the K Cash creative had **no close widget at all** (UI trees
  prove it: `content-desc="Close"` appears only in poll 13 of the run). `_pick()` fell back to
  remembered `known_point` coordinates and tapped (975,584) inside the video and (1007,152) on the
  AdChoices info icon - neither closes anything, and (1007,152) sits next to `Install`.
- **Change:** `_pick()` now returns only a *visually confirmed* glyph (template/Hough, score >= 0.70,
  corner region); remembered priors are never tapped. When the deadline is due and no confirmed X
  exists, the loop sends `KEYCODE_BACK` (max 3) instead of guessing at ad content.
- **Verified:** `test_back_when_no_close_widget` - prior-only candidate -> zero taps, BACK at 17 s;
  all tests pass.

### P010 - a transient screenshot killed the loop on a live board
- **Files:** `src/device.py`, `src/run_loop.py`
- **Why:** `device.screenshot()` raised `ValueError("black frame")` on a blank `screencap` and the
  exception killed the whole process while a 40 s board was sitting there.
- **Change:** `screenshot()` retries 4x with growing backoff and only raises last; every call site in
  `run_loop.py` goes through `_shot_or_recover()` (display recovery + retry).
- **Verified:** syntax ok; all tests pass.

### P011 - the multi-ad interstitial chain has no early exit (no code change)
- **Files:** none (diagnostic only)
- **Why:** run 013's `Watch Ad` started a 3-creative chain (K Cash -> Shacom -> Blade War) that only
  yielded at poll 13 (~65 s). BACK did nothing (navigated inside the WebView); the X exists only on
  the final creative. The board behind such an ad is dead regardless of close speed.
- **Contrast:** the AdMob-style `Reward granted` ad closed cleanly (detector 1.00, poll 7, board
  returned with 38 s). The badge path works when the ad has a badge.
